<title>SINGAPORE: DBS Bank unit raises paid-up capital.</title>
<headline>DBS Bank unit raises paid-up capital.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>DBS Bank said on Friday its subsidiary DBS China Square Ltd (DBSCS) had raised its issued and paid-up capital of Singapore $65 million by S$550,000.</p>
<p>DBS said 38.5 million and 16.5 million redeemable non-cumulative preference shares of S$0.01 each were issued to DBS Bank and Clover Properties Pte Ltd, respectively for cash at a premium of S$0.99 per share.</p>
<p>Clover is a wholly-owned subsidiary of DBS Land Ltd.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
